1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. Bb5+ Bd7 4. Bxd7+ Qxd7 5. c4 e5 6. O-O (6. Nc3 Nc6 (6... g6 7. d3 Bg7 8. a3 (8. Nd5 Ne7 9. Nxe7 Qxe7 10. O-O Nc6 11. Ne1 f5 12. Nc2 O-O 13. Ne3 Qh4 14. f3 {½-½ Boey,J-Makarichev,S/Amsterdam IBM-B 1974/MCL 08}) 8... Nc6 9. Rb1 Nge7 10. b4 O-O 11. bxc5 dxc5 12. O-O h6 13. Nd5 f5 14. Qb3 b6 15. Bd2 g5 $36 {0-1 Torre,E-Radulov,I/Leningrad izt 1973/IZT (30)}) (6... Ne7 7. d3 Nbc6 8. a3 h6 9. Rb1 a5 10. O-O g6 11. b4 axb4 12. Nd5 Nxd5 13. cxd5 Nd4 14. Nxd4 exd4 15. axb4 $36 {[%cal Gb1b7] ½-½ Keres,P-Grigorian,K/URS-ch41 Moscow 1973/URS-ch (29)}) 7. O-O (7. d3 g6 8. Nd5 (8. a3 Bg7 9. Rb1 Nge7 10. b4 b6 11. O-O O-O 12. Nd5 Nxd5 13. cxd5 Nd4 14. Nxd4 cxd4 15. Bd2 $14 {1-0 Spassky,B-Byrne,R/San Juan cqf 1974/CAND (58)}) 8... Bg7 9. a3 Nge7 10. Rb1 Nxd5 11. cxd5 Nd4 12. Nxd4 exd4 13. b4 f5 14. bxc5 dxc5 15. Qb3 b6 16. O-O fxe4 17. dxe4 Rc8 18. Qc4 O-O $132 {0-1 Tkachiev,V-Ivanchuk,V/London PCA rapid 1994/EXP 42 (50)}) 7... Nge7 8. Nd5 Nxd5 9. cxd5 Nd4 (9... Nb4 10. d3 Be7 11. Ne1 O-O 12. Bd2 f5 13. a3 Na6 14. Nc2 fxe4 15. dxe4 c4 16. Ne3 Nc5 17. Nxc4 Nxe4 $13 {[%csl Rd5] / 0-1 Radulov,I-Smejkal,J/Leningrad izt 1973/IZT (56)}) 10. Nxd4 cxd4 11. d3 Be7 12. Qb3 O-O 13. f4 Rac8 14. Bd2 f6 15. h3 Rc7 16. Rf2 Rfc8 17. Raf1 Rc2 18. g4 a6 19. a4 $14 {1-0 Karpov,A-Ribli,Z/EU-chT Bath 1973/EU-chT (70)}) 6... g6 (6... Nc6 7. Nc3 (7. d3 g6 8. Ne1 Bg7 9. Nc3 Nge7 10. f4 exf4 11. Bxf4 O-O 12. Nc2 f5 13. Qd2 Rf7 14. Bh6 Bxh6 15. Qxh6 Raf8 $13 {½-½ Belkhodja,S-Haik,A/FRA-chT 1991/TD 91\02 (31)}) 7... Nge7 8. d3 g6 9. Bg5 Bg7 10. Nd5 Nxd5 11. cxd5 Nd4 12. Nxd4 cxd4 13. f3 O-O 14. Qb3 f5 15. Bd2 f4 16. Rac1 Rfc8 17. a4 a6 18. Rxc8+ Rxc8 19. Rc1 Rxc1+ 20. Bxc1 Bf8 21. Bd2 g5 22. Qd1 h5 23. b3 Be7 24. Kf1 Kf7 25. Be1 Ke8 {½-½ Radulov,I-Smejkal,J/Amsterdam IBM 1973/MCL 07}) 7. Nc3 Bg7 8. d3 Ne7 9. Nh4 (9. Rb1 Nbc6 10. Bd2 O-O 11. Nd5 Nxd5 (11... Rab8 12. b4 Nxd5 13. exd5 Nxb4 14. Bxb4 cxb4 15. Rxb4 Rfe8 16. Re1 Qc7 17. Qb3 Bh6 18. g3 Re7 19. Rb1 b6 $15 {Schmid,L-Andersson,U/Nice olm 1974/MCD-ol/0-1 (40)}) 12. cxd5 Nd4 13. Nxd4 cxd4 14. Qb3 Rfc8 15. Rbc1 Rxc1 16. Rxc1 Rc8 17. Rc4 Rxc4 18. dxc4 Bf8 19. a4 Be7 20. a5 Bd8 21. f3 Kg7 22. Qc2 b6 23. a6 h6 {Shaked,T-Van Buskirk,C/Reno op 1994/EXT 94op/½-½ (57)}) (9. a3 Nbc6 10. Rb1 O-O 11. b4 Nd4 12. Bg5 f6 13. Be3 f5 14. Bxd4 exd4 15. Nd5 fxe4 16. dxe4 b6 17. Ne1 Rae8 18. b5 $14 {/ Klinova,M-Belakovskaia,A/Erevan olw 1996/EXT 96ch2/1-0 (46)}) 9... O-O 10. f4 exf4 {this is a solid safe move when the big question now is whether a  draw will be reached in 10 moves or in 15 moves?!if black wishes to play, than his move must be 10...f5 with unclear position} (10... f5 $5) (10... Nbc6 $2 11. f5 {[%csl Rg7]}) 11. Bxf4 Nbc6 (11... h6 $5 {this was black's last chance for some play,but black really should mind making a draw in this position} 12. Be3 $5 (12. Nf3 Nbc6 13. Qd2 Kh7 (13... g5 14. Bg3 f5)) 12... Nbc6 13. Qd2 Kh7 14. Rf2 $11) 12. Qd2 f5 13. Bh6 Nd4 (13... fxe4 14. Nxe4 (14. dxe4) 14... Nd4 15. Bxg7 Kxg7 16. Rae1 $11) 14. Bxg7 Kxg7 15. exf5 Nexf5 16. Nxf5+ Rxf5 17. Rxf5 Nxf5 18. Re1 Re8 19. Nd5 Re6 20. Nf4 Rxe1+ 21. Qxe1 Qe7 {now you can see what I mean when I say that after 10...exf4 the question is how fast will a draw be made!} 1/2-1/2

