1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 e5 3. dxe5 Ng4 4. Nf3 Bc5 5. e3 Nc6 6. Nc3 O-O 7. Be2 Re8 8. O-O Ngxe5 9. Nxe5 Nxe5 10. Kh1 $5 {[%csl Ge4,Gf4][%cal Yf2f4,Ye3e4] A rather rare, but promising plan. Instead of developing his  to b2 White opts for central expansion (e4,f4) with a possible -side attack.} (10. b3 d6 (10... a5 11. Bb2 Ra6 12. Na4 Ba7 13. c5 Rh6 14. Qd4 Rg6 15. f4 Nc6 16. Qc3 Qh4 17. Bf3 d6 18. a3 Bg4 19. b4 Bxf3 20. Rxf3 axb4 21. axb4 Qh5 22. Kh1 $36 {[%csl Ra7] ץa7,Priehoda,V-Bartsch,B/2.BLO9697/1997/}) 11. Bb2 a5 12. Qd2 Re6 13. g3 Qd7 14. Nd5 Rh6 15. Nf4 Ng6 16. Qc3 f6 17. Nxg6 hxg6 18. h4 Qh3 19. Rfd1 Bd7 20. Bf3 Bc6 21. Bxc6 bxc6 22. Qd3 g5 23. Qe4 gxh4 24. Qxc6 Rf8 $36 {Lazarev,V-Marchand,F/Geneva op/1997/}) 10... d6 11. Na4 $5 ({The logical and consistent follow-up is} 11. f4 Nc6 (11... Nd7 12. Bd3 Nf6 (12... Bxe3 13. Bxh7+ Kxh7 14. Qd3+ $36) 13. Qf3 Ng4 14. Ne4 (14. Nd1 f5 15. Bd2 Bd7 16. Qxb7 c6 17. Qb3 Qh4 18. h3 Qg3 19. hxg4 Qh4+ 20. Kg1 fxg4 21. Be1 g3 22. Bxg3 Qxg3 $40 {Alekseev,V-Bliumberg,V/Minsk-C/1993/}) 14... f5 15. Ng5 Nf6 16. Bd2 $14 {½,Campos,J-de la Villa,J/ESP-chT/1990/}) 12. e4 (12. Nd5 Ne7 13. Nxe7+ Rxe7 14. Qd3 Qe8 15. f5 Bxe3 16. f6 Re5 17. Bf3 Bxc1 18. Raxc1 gxf6 19. Qd2 Qf8 20. Rc3 c6 21. Bd1 Bf5 22. Rcf3 Bg6 23. Rxf6 d5 24. cxd5 cxd5 25. Bb3 Rd8 $15 {Ricardi,P-Sorin,A/ARG-ch plof/1995/}) (12. Bd3 Qh4 13. Nd5 Bg4 14. Qd2 Bb6 15. b4 Re6 16. Qf2 Qh5 17. Bd2 Rh6 18. Qg3 Be2 19. Bc3 Qxh2+ 20. Qxh2 Rxh2+ 21. Kxh2 Bxd3 22. Rfc1 Re8 23. Bd2 Be4 24. a4 a5 25. Nxb6 cxb6 26. bxa5 bxa5 27. Ra3 f5 28. Rb3 Re6 $44 {Doering,T-Huelsmann,J/2BLW/1991/}) 12... Bd4 (12... Nd4 13. Bd3 f5 14. Be3 (14. exf5 Nxf5 15. Ne4 Qh4 16. Qf3 Nd4 17. Qg3 Qxg3 18. Nxg3 Bd7 19. Bd2 Nc6 $11 {½,Andresen,S-Seyb,D/2.BLO/1992/}) 14... g6 15. b4 Bb6 16. Nd5 fxe4 17. Nxb6 Nf5 18. Nd5 c6 19. Be2 cxd5 20. Qxd5+ Be6 21. Qd2 Nxe3 22. Qxe3 Bf7 23. f5 $40 {Poltl,T-Thallinger,G/AUT-ch qual/1991/}) 13. Bd3 (13. Bd2 Bxc3 14. Bxc3 Rxe4 15. Bd3 Re3 16. Qd2 $44 {½,Lukacs,P-Forintos,G/Budapest/1990/}) 13... Bxc3 (13... Qh4 14. Nd5 Re6 15. f5 Be5 16. g3 Bxg3 17. Qe2 Ne5 18. fxe6 Nxd3 19. exf7+ Kf8 20. Bg5 Qxg5 21. Qxd3 Be5 22. Nxc7 Qh4 23. Qc2 Bh3 24. Nxa8 Bxh2 25. Qxh2 Qxe4+ 26. Kg1 Qg4+ 27. Kf2 Qd4+ 28. Ke1 Bg4 29. Qf4 {1-0,Varga,Z-Kahn,E/Zalakaros op/1995/}) 14. bxc3 f5 15. exf5 Qf6 16. Rb1 Bxf5 17. Rxb7 Rec8 18. Be3 Rab8 19. Rb5 Bxd3 20. Qxd3 Qf7 21. Rf5 Qe6 22. Rg5 Re8 23. Bd4 Nxd4 24. Qxd4 g6 25. f5 $16 {Baburin,A-Kahn,E/HUN-chop Gyor/1990/}) 11... b6 $1 $146 {The only way to keep tension in the position.} ({Black has an unpleasant and lifeless position after} 11... Qh4 $143 $6 12. Nxc5 dxc5 13. b3 b6 14. Bb2 Bb7 15. Bxe5 Rxe5 16. Bf3 Bxf3 17. Qxf3 Qe4 18. Rfd1 Qxf3 19. gxf3 Kf8 20. Rd3 Rae8 21. Rad1 g6 22. f4 Re4 23. Rd5 c6 24. Rd7 R8e7 25. Kg2 b5 26. Kf3 $16 {,Xia Yu-Gamsa,M/Beijing Lee Cup/1996/}) 12. Bd2 a5 13. Nxc5 (13. a3 Bd7 $132 {} 14. b4 $2 Bxa4 15. Qxa4 axb4 $19) 13... bxc5 14. f4 (14. Bc3 Bb7 $13) 14... Nd7 15. Bf3 Rb8 $6 {[%csl Ra5] ×a5} (15... Ra7 $142 $1 $13) 16. Qc2 (16. Bxa5 Rxb2 17. Bc3 Rb8 $132 {[%csl Rc4,Re3][%cal Rc8a6] a6,×c4,e3}) (16. b3 $5 a4 17. bxa4 Nb6 18. Qc2 Be6 19. Be2 $14) 16... a4 17. Rae1 Nf6 18. Bc3 (18. Bc1 Rb4 $1 $13) 18... Ng4 19. e4 (19. Bxg4 Bxg4 20. Qxa4 Bf5 $44 {[%csl Rc3,Ge4][%cal Rf5e4] e4}) 19... Qh4 20. h3 a3 21. b3 (21. bxa3 $5 $14) 21... Nh6 22. f5 $5 {} (22. Qd2 Bb7 23. e5 Nf5 $1 $132) 22... f6 $8 (22... Qe7 23. f6 $40) 23. Kh2 Nf7 24. g3 Qh6 25. Bd2 g5 26. h4 Qg7 (26... Bb7 $5 27. Bc1 Ra8 $13) 27. Bc1 Bb7 (27... Ra8 $2 28. e5 $18) 28. Bxa3 Ne5 $132 29. Bh5 (29. Bg2 gxh4 30. gxh4 Qg4 31. Re3 Kh8 $44) 29... Re7 30. Bc1 (30. Bd1 Rbe8 $13 {[%csl Re4][%cal Ge7e4] e,×e4}) 30... g4 {[%csl Rh5] ץh5} 31. Bf4 Kh8 $1 {Black resists the temptation to gain the exchange and retains his powerful e5.} (31... Nf3+ 32. Rxf3 gxf3 33. Bxf3 $14 {[%cal Rg3g5] g4-g5}) 32. Qd2 (32. Bxe5 $5 dxe5 $1 (32... Rxe5 $6 33. Rf4 $16) 33. Qf2 (33. Qe2 Rg8 34. Qe3 Rd7 {d4}) 33... Rd8 34. Qxc5 Red7 $14 {[%cal Gd7d1] d} (34... Rd4 $5)) 32... Rd7 33. Qc3 (33. Bxe5 $6 dxe5 34. Qe3 Rd4 $17 {[%csl Re4] ×e4}) 33... Re7 34. a3 Rg8 35. b4 {The only way to make progress. But now the position opens up and a sharp tactical fight ensues.} cxb4 36. axb4 Ra8 37. Rf2 Qg8 38. c5 $6 ({This was the last chance to exchange e5-} 38. Bxe5 $142 dxe5 (38... Rxe5 39. Rf4) 39. Rd2 $36) 38... Ra2 39. Ree2 (39. Rxa2 $2 Qxa2+ 40. Kh1 Nf3 $1 41. Qxf6+ Kg8 $19) 39... Rxe2 40. Rxe2 Bxe4 $1 41. Rxe4 {Leads to a draw.} ({White can achieve the same result by} 41. Bxe5 Rxe5 42. Rxe4 Rxe4 43. Qxf6+ Qg7 44. Qd8+ Qg8 45. Qf6+ $11) 41... Nf3+ 42. Kh1 Rxe4 43. Qxf6+ Qg7 44. Qd8+ Qg8 45. Qxg8+ (45. Qf6+ Qg7 $11) (45. Qxc7 $4 Re2 $19) 45... Kxg8 46. f6 Re2 $5 (46... Rxf4 47. gxf4 dxc5 48. bxc5 Nxh4 49. Kh2 Nf5 50. Bxg4 Nd4 $11) 47. f7+ Kg7 $8 48. Bh6+ $8 Kxh6 49. f8=Q+ Kxh5 50. Qf5+ (50. Qf7+ Kh6 51. Qf6+ Kh5 $11) 50... Kh6 (50... Kh6 51. Qf4+ Kh5 $11) 1/2-1/2

