1. d4 Nf6 2. c4 g6 3. Nc3 Bg7 4. e4 d6 5. Be2 O-O 6. Bg5 c5 7. d5 e6 (7... h6 {is preferred by theory to avoid the loss of the diagonal c1-h6.} 8. Bf4 (8. Be3 e6) 8... e6) 8. Qd2 Re8 (8... exd5 9. exd5 $1 (9. cxd5 Re8 {is a good Benoni for Black because of the bad  on e2.}) 9... Re8 10. Nf3 {transposes to the game continuation.}) 9. Nf3 exd5 10. exd5 Bg4 11. O-O Nbd7 12. h3 Bxf3 13. Bxf3 a6 14. a4 Qe7 15. Rae1 Qf8 16. Bd1 $1 {The  belongs to the b1-h7 diagonal, and in the long run White will get a space advantage on the kingside after g2-g4 and f2-f4.} Rxe1 (16... h6 17. Bf4 Nh7 18. Bc2 Ne5 19. b3 f5 20. Bg3 Qf6 21. Ne2 $14 {Yusupov-Zapata, Saint John op-2 1988}) 17. Rxe1 Re8 18. Bf4 (18. Rxe8 Qxe8 19. Bc2 Nb6 (19... h5 20. Bf4 Ne5 21. Qe2 Kh7 22. Bd2 Ned7 23. f4 Qxe2 24. Nxe2 Ne8 25. b3 $14 {Doroshkievich-Liberzon, Riga 1970}) 20. b3 Nbd7 21. Bf4 Qe7 22. Qe2 Kf8 23. Qxe7+ Kxe7 24. a5 $14 {Polugaevsky-Uhlmann, Amsterdam 1970}) 18... Rxe1+ 19. Qxe1 Qe8 20. Bd2 Kf8 21. Qxe8+ Nxe8 {After exchanging the heavy artillery White maintains a small, but durable advantage in the endgame. His pair of bishops and the space advantage secure him the better chances.} 22. g4 {This is the typical move here. White has a rather good score in this type of endgame. However this allows 22...a5} (22. a5 $1 {fixing the weaknesses and only after g2-g4 looks more precise.}) 22... Ke7 (22... a5 23. Nb5 b6 {blocks the queenside completely.}) 23. Kg2 (23. a5 $1) 23... a5 {White usually avoids this by playing a4-a5 in time.} 24. Nb5 Bxb2 $2 (24... b6 25. b3 {and Black's position is still a tough nut to crack.}) 25. Bxa5 {Now White has again play on both wings, therefore the pair of bishops is more valuable.} g5 $2 {This helps only for White to open up the position. It was better to sit and wait.} 26. Bd2 h6 27. f4 $1 Bf6 28. Be2 (28. Bb3) 28... gxf4 29. Bxf4 Bg5 30. Bg3 {Certainly White has to avoid the exchange of the bishops.} Bd2 31. Bh4+ f6 (31... Bg5) 32. Bg3 Nb6 33. Bd3 Kf7 $2 (33... Nxa4 34. Bg6) 34. Bxd6 Nxa4 35. Bg3 Nc3 36. d6 Ng7 37. Nc7 Na4 38. Bg6+ Kf8 39. Nd5 Nb2 40. d7 Ne6 41. Bd6+ Kg7 42. Bf5 1-0

