1. c4 {Baburin,A} e6 2. d4 Nf6 3. Nc3 Bb4 4. Qc2 Nc6 5. Nf3 d5 6. cxd5 exd5 7. Bg5 h6 8. Bxf6 Qxf6 9. e3 O-O 10. a3 (10. Be2 $5 Ne7 11. a3 Bd6 12. Nb5 Bf5 13. Qb3 (13. Bd3 Bxd3 14. Qxd3 Nf5 $11 15. h4 $6 (15. Nxd6 Nxd6 16. Ne5 Ne4 17. O-O $11) 15... Rfe8 16. Rh3 c6 17. Nc3 h5 $15 {[%csl Rh3] Kharlov,A-Gogichaishvili,G/URS-Army Khabarovsk 1990/½-½ (49)}) 13... Be4 $5 14. Rc1 c6 15. Nxd6 Qxd6 16. O-O Rab8 $11 {Graf,S-Opocensky,K/Prague 1937 (46)}) 10... Bxc3+ (10... Bf5 $5 11. Bd3 Bxc3+ 12. Qxc3 (12. bxc3 $5 Ne7 13. O-O c6 14. c4 dxc4 15. Bxf5 Nxf5 16. Qxc4 Rfe8 $11 {Wegner,H-Reeh,O/BL 1990/1-0 (74)}) 12... Bg4 (12... Bxd3 $5 13. Qxd3 Nd8 14. Ne5 Re8 15. b4 $14) 13. Be2 Rfe8 14. O-O Re7 15. Rfe1 Nd8 16. Ne5 Bxe2 17. Rxe2 Ne6 $11 {Zigouris-Ivanovic/Korfu op/SW,38,17 1990 (64)}) 11. Qxc3 Bg4 (11... Qg6 12. b4 a6 13. g3 Bg4 14. Bg2 (14. Nd2 $5 $14) 14... Bxf3 $5 15. Bxf3 Qf5 16. Bg2 Rad8 17. O-O Rd7 18. a4 $14 {Lazarev,V-Naumkin,I/Festival Porto San Giorgio 1997/EXP 59/½-½ (45)}) 12. Nd2 $5 (12. Be2 Rfe8 13. O-O Qd6 14. Rac1 Re7 15. Rfe1 Rae8 $11 {Lindblom,P-Kolarov,A/Moscow olm 1956/MCD-ol (22)}) 12... Rae8 (12... Nxd4 $2 13. f3 $18) 13. Nb3 Re7 $1 {Protecting a pawn on c7 and giving the knight a possibility to move.} 14. Bb5 ({Baburin: Perhaps, White should have preferred} 14. Bd3 {Baburin,A ,as the knight on c6 is misplaced, and Black would have to relocate it anyway.}) 14... Nd8 15. O-O c6 16. Bd3 Ne6 $11 {Both sides has finished development and we can see that black easily solved all opening problems.} 17. Rfc1 Rc8 {Planing to simplify the position,while very serious attention deserved} (17... Rfe8 $5 18. Nd2 Bf5 19. Bxf5 Qxf5 20. b4 Ng5 21. a4 Re6 $132) 18. Nd2 c5 $5 {Baburin: This is the easiest way to equalise here, as Black's pieces are ready for the break in the centre.} 19. dxc5 Qxc3 20. Rxc3 Rxc5 21. Rac1 {Actually offering a draw.Better was} (21. Rxc5 $1 Nxc5 22. Bc2 (22. Bb5 {Baburin,A does not give White any hope for an edge either after} a6 23. Rc1 Ne6 {with a further ...d4.}) 22... Rc7 23. f3 Nd7 $1 24. Bb3 Be6 25. Kf2 $14) 21... Rxc3 22. Rxc3 d4 23. exd4 Nxd4 24. f3 Ne2+ 1/2-1/2

